% ============================================================================
% sentence-type.query.adj — a worked recall over the sentence-type library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what kind of sentence
% is this?": it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded
% table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `sentence_type` rows and returns the type + the table's own
% source/locator/trust. An example the table does not carry abstains
% honestly — the engine never invents a classification.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli sentence-type.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "sentence-type.adj"

? sentence_type(bears_dont_eat_when_they_hibernate, $Type)   % expect declarative
? sentence_type($Example, imperative)                        % expect sweep_the_floor_before_you_mop_it
? sentence_type(the_cat_sat_on_the_mat, $Type)                % expect abstain — no type is shipped for this sentence
